1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,220
In this lesson, you'll set up a community
in Kyntlo: a private space where your

2
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:09,820
members can talk, learn and support each
other, right alongside your courses.

3
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:13,525
A good community keeps members
engaged, and keeps them paying.

4
00:00:14,374 --> 00:00:16,428
Communities live in Memberships.

5
00:00:16,428 --> 00:00:18,547
Each community is made of groups.

6
00:00:18,547 --> 00:00:22,720
Think of a group as your own
private social network, with no ads,

7
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:25,674
and no algorithm deciding
who sees your posts.

8
00:00:25,674 --> 00:00:28,177
Every member sees everything you share.

9
00:00:29,028 --> 00:00:32,450
To start a new one, click
Create Group and give it a name.

10
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:35,400
It gets its own web address
on your member portal,

11
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:38,468
the same place members log
in to watch your courses.

12
00:00:39,319 --> 00:00:40,628
Choose who can join.

13
00:00:40,628 --> 00:00:43,638
A private group is only
for people you invite,

14
00:00:43,638 --> 00:00:46,517
or people who buy an
offer that includes it.

15
00:00:46,517 --> 00:00:49,592
A public group is open
to anyone with the link.

16
00:00:49,592 --> 00:00:51,163
Then click Create group.

17
00:00:52,013 --> 00:00:56,088
Your new group starts with a general
channel, ready for its first post.

18
00:00:56,088 --> 00:01:00,047
Let's go back and look at an
established group, the Bloom Smile Club,

19
00:01:00,047 --> 00:01:02,630
from the offer we created
in the last lesson.

20
00:01:03,479 --> 00:01:08,898
Along the top are the group's sections:
the feed, learning, members, a leaderboard,

21
00:01:08,898 --> 00:01:10,531
events and an about page.

22
00:01:10,531 --> 00:01:15,101
On the left are channels, which keep
conversations organised by topic.

23
00:01:15,951 --> 00:01:20,726
Channels can be open to everyone, or
limited to admins, like Announcements,

24
00:01:20,726 --> 00:01:24,291
so important news never gets
buried under everyday chat.

25
00:01:25,141 --> 00:01:29,862
To add one, click the plus next to Channels,
give it a name, choose who can post,

26
00:01:29,862 --> 00:01:30,678
and create it.

27
00:01:32,303 --> 00:01:33,307
Now let's post.

28
00:01:33,307 --> 00:01:36,852
Click the composer, and add
a title and your message.

29
00:01:36,852 --> 00:01:39,395
You can attach images, files or video.

30
00:01:39,395 --> 00:01:41,870
Click Post, and members are notified.

31
00:01:41,870 --> 00:01:45,951
Pin your most important posts,
so new members see them first.

32
00:01:46,770 --> 00:01:49,639
The Learning tab links
your courses to the group,

33
00:01:49,639 --> 00:01:53,855
so members can watch a lesson and
then talk about it, in the same place.

34
00:01:53,855 --> 00:01:56,959
Discussion helps people
actually use what they learn.

35
00:01:57,810 --> 00:02:00,079
And on the right is the leaderboard.

36
00:02:00,079 --> 00:02:03,545
Members earn points for
posting, commenting and liking.

37
00:02:03,545 --> 00:02:07,011
A little friendly competition
keeps people coming back.

38
00:02:07,011 --> 00:02:11,863
You can even reward the top members,
like a free whitening top-up each month.

39
00:02:12,714 --> 00:02:17,928
To grow your group, click Invite members,
and share the link or send email invites.

40
00:02:17,928 --> 00:02:22,200
Or include the group in a paid
offer, and buyers join automatically.

41
00:02:23,051 --> 00:02:24,127
Here's a pro tip.

42
00:02:24,127 --> 00:02:25,963
Communities thrive on rhythm.

43
00:02:25,963 --> 00:02:30,775
Post one simple question every week,
like, share your smile win of the week,

44
00:02:30,775 --> 00:02:32,421
and reply to every answer.

45
00:02:32,421 --> 00:02:36,790
Within a month, your members will
start the conversations themselves.

46
00:02:36,790 --> 00:02:40,082
That's when a community
really starts to run itself.

47
00:02:40,932 --> 00:02:43,396
That's the end of the Memberships module.

48
00:02:43,396 --> 00:02:43,997
Well done!

49
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:47,063
Next, in module fourteen,
we'll head into Settings,

50
00:02:47,063 --> 00:02:49,587
starting with phone numbers and caller ID.

51
00:02:49,587 --> 00:02:50,428
See you there.
